 "note": "Man weak-side help shade ON by default (2026-09-22). A man off-ball HELP defender (posture normal/loose) now sags toward the rim he is defending, scaled by how weak-side he is: the one rim-ward term becomes HELP_BASKET_SHADE x (1 + weakness), so the strong side and a central ball are unchanged (0.20) and the far weak side doubles (0.40). `weakness` is help_side_weakness, EXTRACTED from _apply_zone_help_shade so zone and man share one ramp (zone_sink.SIDE_SPAN + ball_centrality) - no new constant, no clamp, nothing retuned. Deny (tight), the inside-man lock and the on-ball cushion are untouched. Weak-side defender->rim 13.25 -> 10.71, strong side 15.24 -> 14.94, HELP_ANCHOR_FLOOR bind rate FALLS 27.3% -> 25.8%. BOTH footings move: unlike the zone help shade, man defense exists at SEED_DEFENSES=0 too (an empty catalogue makes every zone call play man), so the SD=0 cells are NOT byte-identical to the superseded file. Reproduce the superseded reference with GOB_MAN_HELP_SHADE=0 (verified 40/40 on fp AND draws, all four cells, before the re-cut). See reports/man-help-shade-flip-2026-09-22.md.",
